const mkRules = (base) => 'Read docs/northstar/plans/workflows_2026-10-07/rules.md first (git show origin/main:docs/northstar/plans/workflows_2026-10-07/rules.md); your role\'s section is your rule set; stage files by name only, never git add -A or commit -a; commit messages end with the line Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>. Rules: model Sonnet 5.5; never spawn sub-agents; think tersely; your last message is the report, no interim notices; report once, in the schema. Run no command that can raise a permission prompt (Westley 2026-10-13): the target of rm, git worktree remove and kill is always a literal, fully written-out path (no $VAR, glob or $(...) there); if a command might be destructive or unresolvable, do not run it, leave the item and list it in your report. Worktree ONLY by absolute path: git -C ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold fetch -q && git -C ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold worktree add -b <branch> ~/Projects/om-push/wt/<suffix> ' + base + ' (if that fails, stop and report; never run git with the live checkout as the working tree; the base is ' + base + '). Never touch ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold itself. No stash/rebase/amend/force; never make clean; never push to main. Build: make && make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg (a fresh worktree has no pipe/ouroboros_pipe; the transport tests skip without it, so a skipped transport test is a FAIL of your step). Python ~/Projects/ouroboros-manifold/.venv/bin/python (it lacks jsonschema: use ~/Projects/agora/.venv/bin/python only for a test that imports it). Long runs inside systemd-run --user --scope -q -p MemoryMax=6G -p MemorySwapMax=0 -- nice -n 10 <cmd>. Builders never edit tests; a test that looks wrong stops the piece with stop_reason "test-defect: <test id> | <failing assertion line> | <the ruling or gap line it contradicts, file:line>". Named drafts and rulings are taken as written; anything else undecided stops the piece. Determinism: plain integer arithmetic, no libm transcendentals, no wall clock, no hash-order iteration. This piece changes NO ABI, NO save format, NO checksum, NO header, NO signatures.toml row, NO om_internal.h, NO ledger line and NO client file (autoload/, scenes/, c_bridge.gd): any of those is a STOP. Stop and report (ok=false, stop_reason) on a file outside your list, a number nobody gave (a value from the paragraph, a gap ruling, or an existing constant with file:line is given), a file outside the three files of the pieces.toml row VG-CONTRACT-force-groups owns, a pipe frame other than the one mission frame, or a new symbol. Never stage *.import or *.uid; delete untracked *.uid before any checkout or merge. Pre-gate before every push (rules.md section (a)): MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<worktree>/docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <worktree> ' + base + ' ' + PIECES + ' <your test paths> must end "PRE_GATE verdict OK"; quote the verdict. Ledger merge conflicts keep both sides. Push your branch, write .wt-done (date, branch, sha). Stop past 120k context.'
