// The interface fixed in full for the test writer, the docs agent, the builder and the checkers. A line marked [Gn] is completed by that gap's ruling and the ruling WINS.
const IF = 'INTERFACE (fixed; every agent uses exactly this):\n' +
  '  Frame: the `mission` frame (written by static void write_mission in csrc/pipe/om_pipe.c, answered by mission_start) carries force = {"types":[6 ints],"tiers":[6 ints],"groups":[n ints]} [G4: groups after tiers]. n = sum(types) = the number of tally entries that were counted: the tally loop skips an entry when om_mission_get_force_unit fails or its type is outside 0..5, and a skipped entry contributes nothing to types, tiers or groups. groups[i] is the start group of the i-th counted entry in the TALLY ORDER, which is the player\'s units in ASCENDING UNIT ID order (the join: groups[i] belongs to the i-th player unit by id; the frame carries no unit ids; the client joins against the tactical frame\'s player units sorted by id). The value of each entry is per [G2]: om_mission_get_force_group(W, u) verbatim, range 0 to 3 (0 = no group, the accessor\'s stub sentinel until VG-E-startforce lands; 1 to 3 after). An empty force gives "groups":[]. The key is always present (the frame fields are "always all present"). No other frame, key or verb changes. The ints are written with jb_int; no number is invented (no buffer bound that nobody gave: use a second pass over the same u with the identical skip test, or a second jbuf appended inside the loop, and say which).\n' +
  '  C: NO header, signatures.toml, ABI, save-format, checksum or om_internal.h change. The pipe calls the PUBLIC accessor int32_t om_mission_get_force_group(const om_world *w, uint32_t i) (csrc/ouroboros_sim.h:1810, E7\'s declared stub, ABI 8 unchanged) with i = the tally loop index u. It does not implement or change the accessor (csrc/mission.c is VG-E-startforce\'s).\n' +
  '  Docs: docs/architecture.md: (1) the `force` bullet at :304 gains the `groups` field as this clause, written VERBATIM (it covers what the field is, the length rule, the tally order, the join rule, the value rule and the FU-E7-force-frame sentence): "' + ARCH_CLAUSE + '"; (2) the whole-frame example at :290 carries groups [G3, G5]; (3) the "Wiring status" paragraph after the mission frame list says what groups carries today per [G2] and that no client reads it until VG-A-startforce (approved, not integrated); (4) a short paragraph "VG-CONTRACT-force-groups (2026-10-20, the mission frame names each starting unit\'s control group)" in the style of the neighbouring contract paragraphs: the field, the join, the value rule, no ABI bump (the accessor rides E7\'s ABI 8), the save/checksum statement per [G1] (no bump, nothing saved or hashed), the customers VG-E-startforce (placement) and VG-A-startforce (client binds control groups 1 to 3), See also the pin test and TD-VG-E-31. Rewrite, never append; grep the file for every other sentence the change makes false.'

const ruler = (r) => agent(RULES + '\nRole: ruler (Engineer), rules.md section (e). Builder branch origin/' + r.branch + ' stopped with: ' + r.stop_reason + '\nSpec: ' + SPEC + '. Rulebook: docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-rulebook.md (its "Decision procedure" word for word; the ledger row is TD-VG-E-31, which already exists in push_ledger_2026-09-22.md: a ruling that needs a different row id is ruled false). Branch push/vg-cfg-rulings (suffix vg-cfg-rulings; continue it from origin if it exists: worktree add ~/Projects/om-push/wt/vg-cfg-rulings origin/push/vg-cfg-rulings then git checkout -B push/vg-cfg-rulings, else from ' + BASE + '). If every condition of the procedure holds: edit only the one test file named, run it alone and its positive control, push, report ruled true with row and branch. Else report ruled false and brief (under one page: test id and failing line, the builder\'s claim, the ruling and gap lines that bear on it, two or three options with what each changes). A threshold, window or tolerance is never ruled. A test-defect claim that contradicts a closed ruling (GAP 1 or 2, closed by the spec paragraph) is ruled false. This piece owns no ledger file: a ruling that needs a ledger append is ruled false with the row text in the brief.', { label: 'rule:' + r.branch, phase: 'Build', schema: RULING, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const withRuling = async (mk) => {
  let r = await mk('')
  if (r && !r.ok && /^test-defect:/.test(r.stop_reason || '')) {
    const v = await ruler(r)
    if (v && v.ruled && v.branch) { r = await mk(', origin/' + v.branch + ' (ruling ' + v.row + ')'); r = { ...r, ruling: v } } else { r = { ...r, ruling: v } }
  }
  return r
}

