const mkDocs = () => done('docs') || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Engineer, docs piece for VG-CONTRACT-force-groups of ' + SPEC + '. Branch push/vg-cfg-docs, suffix vg-cfg-docs, from ' + BASE + '. Edit ONLY ' + DOC_FILES.join(' and ') + '. Rewrite, never append (CLAUDE.md stale-doc tripwire). Write exactly what the INTERFACE below and the gap rulings say (the :304 clause verbatim as ARCH_CLAUSE gives it), no number the paragraph or a gap does not give; the example values are the GAP 3 values and are marked as a worked example derived from the split rule. Placement: the :304 bullet and the clause in place (find the `force` bullet of the mission frame list by its words "types` is six counts"), the :290 example in place, the wiring-status paragraph in place, the new paragraph after the neighbouring contract paragraphs in the order of the file (find where the latest VG-CONTRACT paragraph sits; do not reorder anything). State plainly: nothing player-visible changes, no client reads groups until VG-A-startforce (approved, not integrated), and no ABI, save or checksum change per the GAP 1 ruling (no bump, nothing saved or hashed). grep the file for the stale phrases `"tiers":[2,2,1,0,0,0]}`, "tiers` is six tiers", "force.tiers", "two fields", "No pipe frame" and quote what remains and why it is still true. Pre-gate with piece ids ' + PIECES + ' (docs only; the doc lints must pass). Report ok, branch, sha, summary (every architecture.md line you changed, the grep results).\n' + IF + '\n' + RULED, { label: 'docs:CONTRACTforcegroups', phase: 'Docs and Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const mkTests = () => done('tests') || agent(RULES + '\nRole: test writer (Engineer), rules.md section (d), for VG-CONTRACT-force-groups of ' + SPEC + ' (a DIFFERENT agent from the docs agent and from the builder). Branch push/vg-cfg-tests, suffix vg-cfg-tests, from ' + BASE + ' (the built tree: no groups key in the frame, ABI ' + ABI_BASE + '). Edit ONLY ' + TEST_FILES.join(', ') + ' and no source file. QUOTE THE RULE (rules.md section (d)): the file docstring quotes word for word the frame sentence "' + FRAME_SENTENCE + '", Westley\'s words ' + WH + ', and the GAP 2 and GAP 1 rulings (both closed by the paragraph, quoted), and names TD-VG-E-31 and the ids S-105 / R-105-02 where the paragraph does; a case whose behaviour none of these states is not written (report the gap). Write, in this order. POSITIVE CONTROLS first, green on the built tree: (C1) the file\'s detector controls on dict frames: test_check_frame_rejects_todays_empty_frame (its "today" example gains "groups": [] and must STILL be rejected for its original reason: the six-count check on types, quote the failing assertion line) and test_check_frame_accepts_the_documented_example (DOCUMENTED gains groups per GAP 3, i.e. [1, 2, 1, 3, 1] marked as a worked example derived from the paragraph\'s split rule); (C2) new mutate rows in test_check_frame_rejects_each_defect, each breaking one thing alone: groups removed; groups a non-list; groups one entry short; groups one entry long; one entry a bool; one entry a string; one entry the value 4 (the spec\'s named mutant) and one entry -1 (the range is 0 to 3); each is rejected by the new _check_frame (these run on dicts, so they are green today); (C3) the tally-order premise, green today and a premise test, not a feature test: after SET_SEED, START, BEGIN the tactical frame\'s faction-0 units sorted by ascending id have types equal to force.types expanded as [0]*types[0] + [1]*types[1] + ... (premise: the tally order is the player\'s units in ascending id; a red here is a blocking finding, say so). RED CASES, each red on the built tree for the stated reason (the frame has no groups key), the failing assertion line pasted verbatim (file:line and message): (1) the pin at :77 becomes assert set(force) == {"types", "tiers", "groups"}, force (the live tests test_R075_S079_mission_frame_after_set_seed_and_start_is_live and its siblings fail on it today; the pin asserts len(groups) == sum(types) and each int in 0..3); _check_frame gains: groups is a list, every entry an int and not a bool, len(groups) == sum(types), every entry an int in 0..3; (2) a live test: after SET_SEED, START, BEGIN, len(force.groups) equals the number of faction-0 units in the tactical frame, and the same equality in the space-era session the file or tests/transport/test_pipe_vg_e.py already builds (read how; copy the command list, never import from another test module unless this file already does); (3) determinism: two runs give identical groups (the existing deterministic test compares whole frames: confirm it covers groups and say so); (4) the key is present and groups is [] when the force is empty if a session with an empty force exists in the transport tests (premise dumped; else report it as not reachable over the pipe and write nothing). NOTHING asserts a value of 1 to 3 (the stub gives 0; the 1..3 assertion lives in tests/transport/test_pipe_force_groups_values.py, owned by VG-E-startforce, not this piece); NO threshold is invented. Premises are dumped, not assumed: run one real session on the built tree (make && make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg first) and paste the mission frame\'s force object, the faction-0 unit ids and types, the counts; a premise that does not hold is fixed in the test now and said. The ledger row is TD-VG-E-31 (it already exists; write NO ledger line): name it in the docstring as the pin-move row. Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', NEW_TESTS) + '; quote the verdict (red tests make the test step REJECT by design: quote that line and say the other steps are OK). Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the failing lines, the control lines, the dumped premises), red_ids.\n' + IF + '\n' + RULED, { label: 'tests:CONTRACTforcegroups', phase: 'Docs and Tests', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const [docs, tests] = await parallel([mkDocs, mkTests])
out = { ...out, docs, tests }
if (!(docs && docs.ok && tests && tests.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'docs-tests' }

phase('Build')
const mkBuild = (extra) => done('build') || agent(RULES + '\nRole: Doer (rules.md section (a)) for VG-CONTRACT-force-groups of ' + SPEC + ' (the contract is documented in docs/architecture.md on the docs branch; the tests branch holds the red tests). Branch push/vg-cfg, suffix vg-cfg, from ' + BASE + '; merge origin/' + docs.branch + ', origin/' + tests.branch + rulingMerge() + extra + '. Edit ONLY: ' + SRC_FILES.join(', ') + '. Build exactly: in csrc/pipe/om_pipe.c write_mission, the force object gains the groups array after tiers [G4] as the INTERFACE and the G2 ruling say: each counted entry u (the SAME skip test as the tally: om_mission_get_force_unit fails or type outside 0..5 skips) contributes om_mission_get_force_group(W, u) per the G2 ruling (verbatim, 0 to 3), written with jb_int, in the tally order, so the length is exactly sum(types); the closing text becomes ],"groups":[ ... ]}, ; use a second pass over the same u with the identical skip test, or a second jbuf appended inside the loop (no fixed array whose bound nobody gave: OM_MISSION_FORCE_ARRAY_MAX is not visible to the pipe); a comment says "VG-CONTRACT-force-groups: groups[i] is the start group of the i-th counted entry, the player\'s units in ascending id order; See also: tests/transport/test_pipe_mission_frame_briefing_fields.py, docs/architecture.md mission frame" and the same See also at nothing else. NEVER csrc/ouroboros_sim.h, signatures.toml, csrc/mission.c, csrc/om_internal.h, csrc/pipe/pipe_internal.h, csrc/save.c, csrc/checksum_full.c, scripts/specfactory/reach_allowlist.toml, any other pipe handler, any client file. OM_ABI_VERSION stays ' + ABI_BASE + ' (grep it before the push: a change is a STOP).' + RULED + ' STOP RULES: (a) a file outside the list, a number nobody gave, a header or ABI or save change: ok=false, stop_reason says which; (b) a test that looks wrong: test-defect stop per section (a); (c) a libm call, wall clock or hash-order use. Done when ' + NEW_TESTS + ' is fully green on the built tree (make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg first), tests/transport/test_pipe_shapes.py is as green as on the base, scripts/libm_lint.py and scripts/specfactory/alg_constants.py --lint pass if they exist on the tree, scripts/specfactory/reach_lint.py with --base-ref ' + BASE + ' reports nothing new, and the pre-gate ends OK. Pre-gate: ' + PREGATE('<worktree>', NEW_TESTS) + '. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test file PASS/FAIL line, the reach_lint line, the diff stat, which buffer technique), red_ids.', { label: 'build:CONTRACTforcegroups', phase: 'Build', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'doer', model: 'sonnet' })
const build = await withRuling(mkBuild)
out = { ...out, build }
if (!(build && build.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'build' }

phase('Check')
const chk = (suffix, role, body) => () => agent(RULES.replace('worktree add -b <branch>', 'worktree add --detach') + '\nRole: ' + role + ' (Engineer), rules.md section (c), read-only; detached worktrees only (suffix ' + suffix + '; remove after with git worktree remove, no --force). Spec: ' + SPEC + '.\n' + IF + '\n' + RULED + '\n' + body + ' Report pass, blocking, evidence (file:line and the sha read; say what you did not run).', { label: 'check:' + suffix, phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const checks = await parallel([
  chk('chk-cfg-docs-tests', 'gate checker (docs and tests)', 'Detached worktrees at origin/' + docs.branch + ' for the docs and origin/' + tests.branch + ' for the tests. (1) Docs: only docs/architecture.md changed; the :304 bullet states the groups field, the length rule, the tally order, the join rule, the value rule exactly as the G2 ruling says, and the clause at :304 is ARCH_CLAUSE word for word ("' + ARCH_CLAUSE + '"); the :290 example and the wiring-status paragraph agree with it; the new paragraph states no ABI bump (the accessor rides E7\'s ABI 8), the save/checksum statement as the G1 ruling says (no bump, nothing saved or hashed), the customers and "approved, not integrated"; grep for the stale phrases `"tiers":[2,2,1,0,0,0]}`, "two fields", "No pipe frame" and quote what remains and why it is still true. (2) Tests: only ' + TEST_FILES.join(', ') + ' changed, no source, no ledger line; on the base merged with the tests branch the new cases and the moved pin are red for the stated reason (paste the failing lines) and the positive controls are green; the controls break exactly one thing each and fail for that reason (mutate each control back to see the detector accept); the pin lines :77, :97, :103 moved as the TD-VG-E-31 row says; the premise test C3 holds (paste); no assertion of 1 to 3 (range 0..3 and len(groups) == sum(types) asserted); the file docstring quotes the frame sentence, Westley\'s words and the rulings; no threshold invented. (3) Each case is satisfiable: reason through one case per gap ruling.'),
  chk('chk-cfg-build', 'gate checker (build and contract)', 'Detached worktree at origin/' + build.branch + '. (1) The diff versus ' + BASE + ' (git diff --stat) touches ONLY ' + SRC_FILES.join(', ') + ' plus, from the merged branches, the docs and test file (exactly the three files of the pieces.toml row); NOT csrc/ouroboros_sim.h, signatures.toml, mission.c, om_internal.h, pipe_internal.h, save.c, checksum_full.c, reach_allowlist.toml, a ledger file or a client file; OM_ABI_VERSION still reads ' + ABI_BASE + '. (2) The handler change: the groups array uses the same skip test as the tally, written with jb_int after tiers, length == sum(types), no fixed array with an invented bound, public symbols only; run the pipe by hand (SET_SEED, START, BEGIN as the test file does) and paste the real force object and the real tactical frame\'s faction-0 unit count; also with an empty force if the file or a fixture can produce one. (3) ' + NEW_TESTS + ' is green, and RED again with csrc/pipe/om_pipe.c reverted to the base (copy the base file into a scratch copy of the detached tree; never stash). (4) scripts/specfactory/reach_lint.py --base-ref ' + BASE + ' on this tree reports nothing new; libm_lint and alg_constants --lint; tests/transport/test_pipe_shapes.py (validates the live frame against mission.schema.json) as green as on the base. (5) Determinism and read-only: two runs give identical frames; om_world_checksum_full is the same before and after write_mission (if observable through net_checksum or the snapshot checksum, paste both words).'),
  () => agent(RULES.replace('worktree add -b <branch>', 'worktree add --detach') + '\nRole: join checker (Engineer), rules.md section (c), detached worktree at ' + BASE + ' (suffix chk-cfg-join; remove it after with git worktree remove, no --force); merge origin/' + docs.branch + ', origin/' + tests.branch + ', origin/' + build.branch + rulingMerge() + ' into it locally, no push (conflicts mean the lanes overlap: report them). Build (make && make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg); run ' + NEW_TESTS + ', then the whole transport suite, tests/specfactory and the csim tests whose names contain mission, force or briefing; compare the sorted red id list with the base\'s (a detached worktree of ' + BASE + ', suffix chk-cfg-base, built the same way). Expected: identical red lists (nothing new); any new red is COLLATERAL: list it with the decisive line; collateral is not fixed here and fails the check. Wiring (rules: wired, not just tested): a pipe session on the joined tree (mission_start, mission_begin) shows the real force object with groups (paste it) and the length equals the tactical frame\'s player unit count; the accessor is reached from the dispatch chain (reach_lint). Also run the GD tests that read the mission frame (git grep -l mission_frame tests/*.gd; tests/test_briefing_a4_roster.gd, tests/test_briefing_debrief.gd) under scripts/run_godot_tests.sh and say PASS/FAIL (the four FINDING reds ' + RED4 + ' are red on the base and are not this piece\'s). Report pass, evidence (each red id and its decisive line).', { label: 'check:join', phase: 'Check', schema: VERDICT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' }),
])
out = { ...out, checks }
if (checks.some((c) => !(c && c.pass))) return { ...out, stopped: 'check' }

phase('Clerk')
const clerk1 = done('clerk1') || await agent(RULES + '\nRole: landing clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b), part 1: the branch. This clerk runs NO full gate, takes NO gate lock and pushes NOTHING to main. Branch push/vg-cfg-land, suffix vg-cfg-land, from ' + BASE + '; merge origin/' + docs.branch + ', origin/' + tests.branch + ', origin/' + build.branch + rulingMerge() + '. Stage files by name only (never git commit -a, never git add -A, no *.import or *.uid). Build (make && make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg); run ' + NEW_TESTS + ' and list PASS/FAIL. Pre-gate (section (b)): ' + PREGATE('<landing worktree>', NEW_TESTS) + '; it must end OK. NO ledger edit (the owner row has no ledger file; TD-VG-E-31 and FU-E7-force-frame are closed by the Dispatcher\'s record batch, GAP 6). pieces.toml is NOT edited by this clerk. In docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-programme.md edit ONLY the lane-table row that names VG-E-startforce (the E part e row; if none names this piece or VG-E-startforce add nothing and say so): On main "VG-CONTRACT-force-groups built on branch push/vg-cfg-land (from main); not on main until the land clerk lands it", Next piece "the land clerk; then VG-CONTRACT-layerspot and VG-CONTRACT-route, then VG-E-startforce"; write nothing about status anywhere else. No shot and no story_reviews row (nothing player-facing). Commit all of that in one commit (normal prose, Co-Authored-By trailer). Push the branch push/vg-cfg-land. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push and remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin, else leave it with .wt-done. Report ok, branch, sha, summary (the test line, the pre-gate verdict, which predecessors are on main, the ABI reading ' + ABI_BASE + ' unchanged).', { label: 'clerk1:CONTRACTforcegroups', phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, clerk1 }
if (!(clerk1 && clerk1.ok)) return { ...out, stopped: 'clerk1' }
const clerk2 = await agent(RULES_MAIN + '\nRole: land clerk (Engineer), rules.md section (b), part 2: the gate and the push, serialised under the gate lock. ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'The push to main at the end IS authorised on a clean gate (Westley\'s standing word for clean-gate pushes, passed by the Dispatcher), subject to the known-red rule below.' : 'Do NOT push to main (args.pushMain false): branch only.') + ' Branch push/vg-cfg-land (continue it: worktree add -b push/vg-cfg-land-2 ~/Projects/om-push/wt/vg-cfg-land-2 origin/push/vg-cfg-land, suffix vg-cfg-land-2), then merge origin/main (say what moved; ledger, pieces.toml and docs appends keep both sides; any other conflict is a STOP). FIRST, before the merge: read OM_ABI_VERSION on origin/main (git show origin/main:csrc/ouroboros_sim.h); it must read ' + ABI_BASE + ' (the number this piece was built on; the piece changes none); if it reads another number, stop ok=false stop_reason "abi-moved: main reads <n>". Re-check that ' + E7 + ' and ' + E1R + ' are still attached on origin/main (pieces.toml); if either is not, stop ok=false stop_reason "predecessor-not-attached". Stage files by name only (never git commit -a, never git add -A, no *.import, no *.uid). Build (make && make pipe/ouroboros_pipe pipe/ouroboros_pipe_dbg); run ' + NEW_TESTS + ' PASS/FAIL. Pre-gate before the lock (section (b)): MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + ' ' + NEW_TESTS + '; it must end OK (the footprint base is now origin/main: a footprint line naming an unowned file is a STOP). Full gate, EXACTLY section (b), detached, from the landing worktree, the lock taken first and origin/main fetched and merged inside it (main moves while a clerk waits for the lock): mkdir -p ~/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-cfg; flock ~/Projects/om-push/gate.lock env TMPDIR=$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-cfg MERGE_GATE_SUITE_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAYTHROUGH_TIMEOUT=2400 MERGE_GATE_PLAY_TIMEOUT=900 MERGE_GATE_PIECES=<landing worktree>/docs/northstar/plans/push/pieces.toml bash -c \'cd <landing worktree> && git fetch origin && git merge --no-edit origin/main && scripts/specfactory/pre_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + ' && scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh <landing worktree> origin/main ' + PIECES + '\' >$HOME/Projects/om-push/tmp-vg-cfg/gate.log 2>&1 (setsid nohup; three positional arguments to each script; the last is ONE comma list with no spaces; add any further owner id a footprint line names and re-run the pre-gate; the pre-gate above is the cheap early check and pre_gate runs again inside the lock, on the tree after the merge; the script rejects a candidate that lacks the current origin/main, so a forgotten merge costs seconds, not a gate); poll gate.log for the ^GATE look line, one foreground command under 10 minutes at a time, every 5 minutes at most; then pgrep -f \'^bash scripts/specfactory/merge_gate.sh\' to confirm no gate for the worktree still runs (never pgrep your own command line); the verdict is the set of GATE <stage> REJECT lines. Flake rule per section (b). Delete only the merge_gate_before_* directories under your own TMPDIR. KNOWN-RED RULE (section (b), Architect 2026-10-12): push main only when EVERY GATE REJECT line names a test or play listed by exact id in ' + KNOWN_RED_PLAYS + ' or ' + KNOWN_RED_GD + ' on the landing tree; a reject outside those files means branch only, every REJECT line quoted, never a push. The four FINDING-gd-red-main-2026-10-12 tests (' + RED4 + ') may still be red on main until their pieces land: they are listed or they reject; do not fix them. The playthrough stage is the wired check (the pipe frame is written in play); a golden moving is a STOP for the Architect, not a listing. If no REJECT, or only listed ones: flip VG-CONTRACT-force-groups in pieces.toml to status = { state = "attached", attach_sha = "<landing sha7>" } (the format of the attached rows) and rewrite ONLY the programme lane-table row clerk 1 edited: On main "VG-CONTRACT-force-groups at <sha7>: mission.force.groups, the accessor value verbatim (zeros until VG-E-startforce); no ABI bump; approved, not integrated: no client reads it until VG-A-startforce", Next piece "VG-E-startforce". NO ledger edit (owner row); the report names the landing sha for the record batch that closes TD-VG-E-31 and FU-E7-force-frame. Commit (normal prose, Co-Authored-By trailer). Right before the push: git fetch origin; if origin/main moved, merge it in (say so) and re-run the pre-gate and re-read the ABI number; push the branch, then ' + (PUSH_MAIN ? 'git push origin HEAD:main (only under the known-red rule above)' : 'stop at the branch (args.pushMain false)') + '. Write .wt-done (date, branch, pushed sha) after the push and remove the worktree only if it is clean and its HEAD is contained in origin (git branch -r --contains HEAD), else leave it with .wt-done. The report\'s summary carries: the stage lines verbatim ("OK per stage" or every GATE REJECT line), the WARN lines, the test line, main head, the landing sha, and the plain statement "VG-CONTRACT-force-groups: mission.force.groups is built, tested and documented; nothing player-visible changed; approved, not integrated: the readers are VG-E-startforce\'s placement and VG-A-startforce\'s client". Report ok, branch, sha, summary, red_ids.', { label: 'clerk2:CONTRACTforcegroups', phase: 'Clerk', schema: REPORT, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
out = { ...out, clerk2 }
return { ...out, pushMain: PUSH_MAIN, next: 'VG-E-startforce (vg-wave12-laneEstartforce.js: implements om_mission_get_force_group and the pockets; its frame test asserts groups values 1 to 3); then VG-A-startforce (the client binds control groups 1 to 3 from groups). The Dispatcher says: approved, not integrated, nothing player-visible changed, no shot' }
